I&#39;ve got EE, RC/IR, TC, WCos, and Guise. &nbsp;That&#39;s 17 heroes, for 5 games. &nbsp;Plus Steam. &nbsp;Can multiple computers using the same Steam account play the same game at once? &nbsp;If so, my family has got 3 computers that could play it. &nbsp;So 8 games total. &nbsp;Space isn&#39;t a problem - my family has an enormous house. &nbsp;Tokens aren&#39;t a problem either - one of my hobbies is making paper stars, and I have over 25,000, in various colors. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

Hm... Legacy doesn&#39;t have any deck searchers, and very little card draw. &nbsp;Pair him with villains and environments that don&#39;t mill cards from hero decks and play quickly (for example Iron Legacy and Infinitor), and seperate him from heros that allow him extra card draw (Vis or AA) and you could very easily split his deck in two and have Legacy and Young Legacy playing at the same time without any danger of running out of cards. &nbsp;So I&#39;m going to bump that to 9 games.

&nbsp;

[quote="Donner"]

Um...&nbsp; Does a computer and a printer count?&nbsp; I could presumably create a ton of decks by printing them out and then using them...

[/quote]
I would say yes, but that you have to proxy them properly using sleeves and cards from some other game.

Of course, if we allow proxies then you could theoretically play an arbitrarily large number of games using spreadsheets and a random number generator. &nbsp;So maybe we should disallow those.

[quote="Arcanist Lupus"]

Can multiple computers using the same Steam account play the same game at once? &nbsp;If so, my family has got 3 computers that could play it.&nbsp;

[/quote]

I don&#39;t feel like turning on my Laptop to double check if they were all connected to the internet (I want to say no). However, if all but a maximum of 1 is diconnected, they can certainly run it.

&nbsp;

I have the original edition, Enhanced Edition, all expansions, and 2 computers to run the video game. By my calculations, I should be able to run 14 games. The vast majority of the games would be played on the floor. This is assuming I will be the one playing them all solo. It&#39;s tempting to do... Though a 5 year old kid coming down here wouldn&#39;t be a very good outcome.
